Still working on the static version, however, kroc_clock is just your
processor speed, as shown (almost) in /proc/cpuinfo. My values differ by a
tiny amount, but it doesn't seem to matter. So just whack in your
processor speed into that file. For reference, mine looks as follows: 

[alex@aquila fortunes]$ cat /proc/cpuinfo | grep MHz
cpu MHz         : 1460.471
[alex@aquila fortunes]$ cat /etc/kroc_clock
